"""
borescope_setup.py  -  Isaac Sim 6.0.1   (no UI: GUI, web viewer or headless)

Creates the borescope inside the engine with the settings we established, and
prints a report. No windows. To tune, edit the CONFIG block and run it again
(every run deletes and rebuilds /Borescope, so re-running is safe).

  * Port      : measured from the port cutter mesh (centre, axis, diameter, length)
  * Frame     : kinematic-model frame. Origin at the port, +Y = insertion,
                +Z = up (perpendicular to Y), +X = Y x Z
  * Probe     : lambda / theta (= sigma/rho) / alpha / beta, with static gravity sag
                using the stiffness validated in the PhysX bench (EI/w = 4.4687e-3 m^3)
  * Camera    : calibrated OpenCV pinhole + Brown-Conrady distortion, 1280x1024.
                Active, but its viewport gizmo is hidden so you only see the probe
  * Tip light : disk LED with a cone, pointing forward

The full interactive version (sliders, view window) is borescope_port_placement.py:
keep it for debugging. Both use the same CONFIG names.

Headless: open the stage first (or set USD_PATH), run this file, then step the app
(simulation_app.update()) a few times before capturing. Set CREATE_RENDER_PRODUCT
= True to get a render product on the borescope camera for capture/streaming.
"""

